WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.969
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:30.239 --> 00:33.719
We need authorization from every single investor.

3
00:34.039 --> 00:35.079
Every single one?

4
00:35.600 --> 00:36.399
How many people is that?

5
00:37.240 --> 00:38.439
We'd have to get everyone to sign.

6
00:38.600 --> 00:40.560
What if even one refuses to sign?

7
00:41.119 --> 00:42.159
It's all Liu Xuemei's fault.

8
00:44.240 --> 00:45.359
The auction fell through,

9
00:45.600 --> 00:46.359
and now she's dead.

10
00:47.240 --> 00:48.560
We still need her authorization.

11
00:49.679 --> 00:50.439
Where on earth do we get that?

12
00:51.200 --> 00:52.880
Hire a shaman to summon her spirit?

13
00:53.960 --> 00:54.600
Why'd you kick me?

14
00:54.799 --> 00:55.439
Cut the crap, both of you.

15
00:55.439 --> 00:56.119
Am I wrong?

16
00:56.119 --> 00:57.280
You're talking complete nonsense.

17
00:57.679 --> 00:58.520
If you ask me,

18
00:59.000 --> 01:00.679
why don't we forge her signature?

19
01:00.840 --> 01:01.840
We sign it for her.

20
01:02.600 --> 01:03.920
Make it look messy on purpose.

21
01:04.000 --> 01:04.760
If anyone asks,

22
01:04.879 --> 01:05.840
we just say the ink smudged.

23
01:06.120 --> 01:06.680
Right!

24
01:06.680 --> 01:07.519
Are you an idiot?

25
01:07.519 --> 01:08.879
Give it a rest, will you?

26
01:08.920 --> 01:10.560
You think the auction folks are stupid?

27
01:10.760 --> 01:11.439
Then what do we do?

28
01:12.079 --> 01:13.319
What about my money?

29
01:13.959 --> 01:14.359
Move, get back!

30
01:14.359 --> 01:14.879
Don't start that here.

31
01:15.280 --> 01:17.200
Worst comes to worst, I'll sue them in court!

32
01:17.799 --> 01:18.239
Right?

33
01:18.239 --> 01:19.079
Sue who?

34
01:19.680 --> 01:20.319
Go to court?

35
01:20.319 --> 01:21.640
Aren't you afraid of getting exposed now?

36
01:21.799 --> 01:23.480
Are you completely out of your mind?

37
01:23.480 --> 01:24.200
Do you have any idea?

38
01:24.239 --> 01:26.319
Lawsuits drag on forever!

39
01:26.599 --> 01:27.799
Before the case even ends,

40
01:27.799 --> 01:28.640
you'll be laid off!

41
01:28.680 --> 01:29.799
You get it, dummy?

42
01:30.000 --> 01:31.159
The factory will be gone,

43
01:31.159 --> 01:32.159
the money will be gone,

44
01:32.159 --> 01:34.480
and we'll have lost everything!

45
01:35.640 --> 01:36.480
No matter what,

46
01:37.319 --> 01:38.200
the list cannot be leaked.

47
01:39.079 --> 01:41.200
Our coworkers trusted us

48
01:41.319 --> 01:42.079
and loved the factory,

49
01:42.439 --> 01:44.040
that's why they put in their life savings.

50
01:44.200 --> 01:44.760
That's right.

51
01:45.120 --> 01:46.239
And if this list gets out,

52
01:46.239 --> 01:46.959
let me tell you,

53
01:47.079 --> 01:48.519
it'll turn straight into a layoff list!

54
01:49.000 --> 01:49.519
You believe that?

55
01:49.519 --> 01:51.680
What if the auction company sold us out?

56
01:51.680 --> 01:53.480
They're bound by strict confidentiality.

57
01:53.560 --> 01:54.959
Breaching that means paying damages!

58
01:55.120 --> 01:55.760
I don't care about any list!

59
01:55.760 --> 01:56.719
I just want my money!

60
01:56.799 --> 01:57.159
Money!

61
01:57.239 --> 01:58.159
Money, money, money!

62
01:58.159 --> 01:59.280
Money is all you ever think about!

63
01:59.879 --> 02:00.599
If we get laid off,

64
02:00.760 --> 02:01.840
someone like you won't starve!

65
02:01.840 --> 02:02.920
Neither of you will starve!

66
02:03.239 --> 02:04.319
What about my coworkers?

67
02:04.599 --> 02:05.200
What will they eat?

68
02:05.840 --> 02:06.439
What will their wives eat?

69
02:06.439 --> 02:07.079
What will their kids eat?

70
02:07.359 --> 02:08.120
What will their families eat?

71
02:08.400 --> 02:08.879
Chunyan!

72
02:09.360 --> 02:10.159
What are you eating?

73
02:12.240 --> 02:13.080
The fundraising list!

74
02:16.159 --> 02:16.680
The list!

75
02:17.520 --> 02:17.960
Chunyan!

76
02:18.560 --> 02:19.360
Spit it out, quick!

77
02:19.360 --> 02:19.879
You can't eat that!

78
02:19.879 --> 02:20.719
Chunyan, spit it out!

79
02:20.759 --> 02:21.520
Water, water, water!

80
02:21.520 --> 02:22.599
Don't give her water! No water!

81
02:23.680 --> 02:25.199
Chunyan! Chunyan! Chunyan!

82
02:26.080 --> 02:26.599
Spit it out!

83
02:26.599 --> 02:27.240
Enough!

84
02:27.520 --> 02:28.560
Quit panicking!

85
02:28.800 --> 02:30.479
Take her to the clinic right away!

86
02:31.479 --> 02:32.240
Wait! Hold on!

87
02:32.240 --> 02:34.240
Pumping her stomach will expose the list!

88
02:34.599 --> 02:35.360
Well... then...

89
02:37.479 --> 02:38.560
I swallowed it.

90
04:21.439 --> 04:22.319
Xiao Tu,

91
04:23.120 --> 04:24.240
you're still too impulsive.

92
04:25.079 --> 04:26.839
What's the point of eating just the list?

93
04:26.879 --> 04:28.279
Isn't there still a ledger?

94
04:29.040 --> 04:30.519
Can't you just shut up?

95
04:32.439 --> 04:33.959
Chunyan did it for all of us!

96
04:35.120 --> 04:35.920
If you get her all worked up

97
04:35.920 --> 04:37.079
and she eats the ledger, it's on you!

98
04:44.279 --> 04:45.720
I've got a win-win solution.

99
04:48.720 --> 04:49.959
We still take the money.

100
04:50.680 --> 04:51.680
Take the cash and wait at home.

101
04:52.920 --> 04:53.600
A strike?

102
04:55.160 --> 04:55.600
Exactly.

103
04:56.759 --> 04:57.480
With nobody working,

104
04:57.480 --> 04:58.360
the plant will shut down.

105
04:59.040 --> 05:00.399
Then he'll definitely have to

106
05:00.399 --> 05:01.399
beg everyone back one by one.

107
05:02.360 --> 05:03.319
Don't you want the money?

108
05:04.040 --> 05:04.480
Let's go.

109
05:07.000 --> 05:07.439
Well... but...

110
05:07.439 --> 05:08.439
Shun'er and I will go get—

111
05:08.439 --> 05:09.160
Where are you two going?

112
05:09.959 --> 05:11.000
To sort out the authorization.

113
05:11.279 --> 05:11.920
Sit down first.

114
05:13.319 --> 05:14.399
He's a college grad.

115
05:14.560 --> 05:15.920
He can find a job anywhere.

116
05:16.199 --> 05:17.240
Where will you two go if you're laid off?

117
05:19.480 --> 05:19.920
Besides,

118
05:21.319 --> 05:23.639
how long can you hold onto this iron rice bowl?

119
05:23.920 --> 05:25.800
How long will this little bit of cash last?

120
05:25.800 --> 05:27.079
Don't you two have any clue?

121
05:27.879 --> 05:28.600
Wait, but...

122
05:28.959 --> 05:29.879
what about the money?

123
05:30.920 --> 05:31.839
What about it?

124
05:32.399 --> 05:33.000
Let me make my stance clear.

125
05:33.560 --> 05:34.240
I don't want the money anymore.

126
05:34.800 --> 05:35.480
Wait, but you just—

127
05:35.480 --> 05:36.120
Fine if you don't want it!

128
05:36.120 --> 05:36.600
What about my money?

129
05:36.600 --> 05:38.120
That's my entire life savings!

130
05:38.120 --> 05:39.639
You can't just be so shortsighted.

131
05:39.639 --> 05:40.439
All my money's gone right now! Alright, alright.

132
05:40.439 --> 05:41.199
Both of you, cut it out.

133
05:41.240 --> 05:41.800
Enough.

134
05:42.040 --> 05:43.160
Just keep it down.

135
05:45.920 --> 05:46.720
What's the point

136
05:46.720 --> 05:48.279
of us bickering like this?

137
05:48.399 --> 05:50.360
So many people pooled their money with us.

138
05:50.600 --> 05:52.040
Shouldn't we see what everyone wants?

139
05:54.360 --> 05:54.800
Right.

140
05:55.879 --> 05:57.000
We have to find a way

141
05:58.800 --> 05:59.959
to get everyone's money

142
06:00.639 --> 06:01.279
all back first.

143
06:01.639 --> 06:02.800
Then we can talk about

144
06:03.360 --> 06:04.959
whether the list gets exposed.

145
06:07.079 --> 06:08.040
Old Chen is right.

146
06:08.360 --> 06:08.639
Right?

147
06:08.639 --> 06:10.560
I—I say let's take a show of hands.

148
06:10.759 --> 06:11.199
Well...

149
06:11.199 --> 06:12.079
for the forklift crew...

150
06:12.120 --> 06:12.800
We... we want the money.

151
06:13.000 --> 06:13.759
Workshop Two wants the money, too!

152
06:28.399 --> 06:29.000
Tieping.

153
06:31.680 --> 06:32.639
Stop playing dumb.

154
06:33.519 --> 06:34.720
What's your side thinking?

155
06:36.959 --> 06:37.639
Don't ask me.

156
06:38.000 --> 06:38.959
I just do what my mentor says.

157
06:50.560 --> 06:51.199
Look,

158
06:52.319 --> 06:53.519
to put it bluntly,

159
06:54.879 --> 06:55.839
that money

160
06:56.839 --> 06:58.079
is everything Tieping and I

161
06:58.879 --> 06:59.879
have in the world.

162
07:01.879 --> 07:02.519
Forget about me.

163
07:03.439 --> 07:05.439
Just take the five thousand Tieping scraped together.

164
07:07.439 --> 07:10.240
Think of how many crates of beer

165
07:11.199 --> 07:12.319
he had to haul to make that!

166
07:13.720 --> 07:14.199
Right?

167
07:17.199 --> 07:18.319
You want your money back,

168
07:19.600 --> 07:20.279
and so do I.

169
07:22.639 --> 07:23.680
But today,

170
07:24.240 --> 07:25.680
if this list is handed over,

171
07:28.040 --> 07:29.199
what will happen to Tieping?

172
07:30.639 --> 07:31.240
Besides,

173
07:32.600 --> 07:33.720
on that list,

174
07:34.000 --> 07:35.120
folks from the bottling workshop,

175
07:35.920 --> 07:36.560
there are plenty of them, right?

176
07:39.040 --> 07:39.920
Among them,

177
07:40.519 --> 07:41.639
some I watched join the plant,

178
07:44.639 --> 07:45.959
and some watched me join.

179
07:47.879 --> 07:49.199
Now you're telling me

180
07:49.319 --> 07:51.040
they can't stay at the plant anymore?

181
07:53.240 --> 07:54.360
They have no other skills.

182
07:56.079 --> 07:57.040
What will they live on?

183
08:00.959 --> 08:01.480
Sure,

184
08:04.040 --> 08:05.360
three or five thousand

185
08:06.199 --> 08:07.000
is a lot of money.

186
08:09.800 --> 08:10.519
Tell me,

187
08:11.560 --> 08:12.720
with just a few thousand,

188
08:13.519 --> 08:14.560
can they really

189
08:15.560 --> 08:16.439
make it last until they die?

190
08:18.079 --> 08:18.680
Can they?

191
08:20.480 --> 08:21.160
Sit down.

192
08:22.839 --> 08:23.439
Qian Yichuan,

193
08:24.839 --> 08:26.120
you started this, didn't you?

194
08:27.279 --> 08:27.879
I did.

195
08:30.839 --> 08:31.920
You went to college.

196
08:32.679 --> 08:33.519
You're educated.

197
08:34.720 --> 08:36.799
You conned us onto your rocket ship.

198
08:38.080 --> 08:39.240
You have a parachute,

199
08:39.279 --> 08:40.919
while the rest of us fall to our deaths!

200
08:41.000 --> 08:41.879
What are you really planning?

201
08:43.960 --> 08:45.320
Now you're duping everyone

202
08:45.720 --> 08:46.799
into going on strike!

203
08:47.559 --> 08:48.320
What's your angle?

204
08:49.320 --> 08:50.559
If everyone gets laid off,

205
08:50.960 --> 08:52.200
what do you get out of it?

206
08:52.720 --> 08:54.200
You want to be the plant director?

207
08:55.879 --> 08:56.559
Qian Yichuan,

208
08:58.320 --> 09:00.080
you don't deserve to work at Lapi Brewery!

209
09:01.480 --> 09:02.720
Lao Cheng, Lao Cheng!

210
09:03.000 --> 09:04.080
Calm down, take it easy!

211
09:04.639 --> 09:05.159
Sit, sit, sit.

212
09:05.320 --> 09:05.759
Sit down.

213
09:05.960 --> 09:06.440
Sit down.

214
09:12.919 --> 09:13.759
Bottling workshop!

215
09:17.440 --> 09:18.279
Back to work!

216
09:28.200 --> 09:28.519
Hey,

217
09:28.519 --> 09:29.799
forklift crew, let's get back to work too.

218
09:30.159 --> 09:30.720
You want to get laid off?

219
09:30.720 --> 09:31.080
Get moving!

220
09:34.320 --> 09:34.759
Liuzi!

221
10:10.120 --> 10:11.320
Your place got broken into?

222
10:12.919 --> 10:13.879
I need to head out for a while.

223
10:14.960 --> 10:16.480
These things...

224
10:16.559 --> 10:17.600
...still mean something to me.

225
10:18.080 --> 10:18.960
I'll leave them with you for now.

226
10:19.600 --> 10:20.720
When did it happen?

227
10:21.360 --> 10:22.120
The night before last.

228
10:22.279 --> 10:23.120
The night before last?

229
10:23.279 --> 10:24.279
Weren't you at my place?

230
10:24.679 --> 10:25.639
What did they steal?

231
10:26.799 --> 10:28.039
Discarded footage from Lapi Brewery.

232
10:30.840 --> 10:31.919
You still kept that?

233
10:33.919 --> 10:35.600
Why would anyone steal that?

234
10:35.720 --> 10:36.600
Who did it?

235
10:38.000 --> 10:39.240
Who else could it be?

236
10:39.759 --> 10:40.360
Who?

237
10:43.759 --> 10:44.519
Leshui is here.

238
10:45.600 --> 10:47.039
I came to see Xiaoqin and Xiaohu.

239
10:47.720 --> 10:48.440
Have you eaten yet?

240
10:48.519 --> 10:49.480
Stay for dinner before you go.

241
10:50.840 --> 10:52.919
Why are you home so early today?

242
10:53.600 --> 10:54.799
Exams are over,

243
10:54.919 --> 10:56.320
so school let out early.

244
10:58.639 --> 10:59.480
What's there to eat?

245
10:59.919 --> 11:00.440
I'm starving.

246
11:01.399 --> 11:01.919
Let me take that.

247
11:03.039 --> 11:03.639
I'll leave you to it, then.

248
11:03.799 --> 11:04.360
I'm heading back.

249
11:04.759 --> 11:05.240
Leaving already?

250
11:05.240 --> 11:05.639
Chen Yuan.

251
11:06.240 --> 11:07.120
Help Leshui take the box...

252
11:07.159 --> 11:08.120
...down to the storage room.

253
11:08.480 --> 11:08.840
Sure.

254
11:09.960 --> 11:11.639
You called the other day saying your camera broke.

255
11:11.639 --> 11:12.120
Here.

256
11:12.679 --> 11:14.279
I was going to have Chen Yuan fix it for you.

257
11:14.279 --> 11:15.000
No need to fix it.

258
11:15.080 --> 11:15.919
I'll just buy a new one.

259
11:16.759 --> 11:17.240
Leshui.

260
11:17.600 --> 11:18.720
It'll be safe here, don't worry.

261
11:19.120 --> 11:19.720
Thanks.

262
11:19.919 --> 11:20.480
I'm off.

263
11:33.600 --> 11:34.240
Miss,

264
11:34.240 --> 11:34.919
what can I get you?

265
11:38.360 --> 11:39.360
Do you have a machine here

266
11:39.720 --> 11:41.200
that can play this kind of tape?

267
11:41.799 --> 11:42.320
Yeah.

268
11:51.919 --> 11:53.120
For an old tape like this,

269
11:53.159 --> 11:54.639
only this kind of player will work.

270
11:56.120 --> 11:56.960
Over the past couple of days,

271
11:57.000 --> 11:58.679
has anyone bought one of these?

272
11:59.519 --> 12:01.080
I think one person did.

273
12:01.480 --> 12:02.360
What did he look like?

274
12:03.039 --> 12:04.759
About thirty or so.

275
12:04.879 --> 12:05.759
Average build.

276
12:05.919 --> 12:06.639
A bit taller than me.

277
12:07.360 --> 12:08.159
Did he look like a cop?

278
12:08.519 --> 12:09.360
A cop?

279
12:10.360 --> 12:11.519
Why are you asking?

280
12:12.679 --> 12:14.679
Just worried I'd buy the same thing as my brother.

281
12:17.759 --> 12:18.480
Sorry about that.

282
12:18.600 --> 12:19.240
Thank you.

283
12:28.320 --> 12:29.399
Hey, were you looking for me?

284
12:29.600 --> 12:29.960
Hey,

285
12:30.120 --> 12:30.919
today I ran into

286
12:30.919 --> 12:32.159
Miao from the station back then.

287
12:32.799 --> 12:33.519
Miao Yuzhu.

288
12:33.519 --> 12:34.120
Remember her?

289
12:34.720 --> 12:35.360
She said back then,

290
12:35.360 --> 12:36.840
she worked with you on Malt Kingdom,

291
12:37.000 --> 12:38.159
helping sort through footage.

292
12:38.279 --> 12:38.679
Director Zheng...

293
12:38.679 --> 12:39.559
She slipped you three extra tapes. You called me?

294
12:40.000 --> 12:40.399
Xiao Miao...

295
12:40.399 --> 12:41.240
She did it behind the boss's back.

296
12:41.240 --> 12:42.080
You took her to fetch the tapes,

297
12:42.080 --> 12:43.200
so she's really fond of you.

298
12:43.840 --> 12:45.080
Miao runs a self-media account now.

299
12:45.159 --> 12:47.320
Almost every article gets over 100k views.

300
12:47.480 --> 12:47.960
She said

301
12:47.960 --> 12:50.080
if you have any explosive scoops,

302
12:50.360 --> 12:51.440
she'd love to publish them for us.

303
12:54.399 --> 12:55.559
I never even considered that.

304
12:56.679 --> 12:58.320
Lives are on the line here.

305
12:59.200 --> 13:00.279
Investigating is fine,

306
13:00.720 --> 13:02.200
but we can't interfere with police work.

307
13:03.039 --> 13:04.759
As journalists, we must be responsible.

308
13:06.679 --> 13:07.480
Got it.

309
13:07.879 --> 13:08.679
That you're willing to mentor me...

310
13:08.679 --> 13:09.679
I'm truly touched.

311
13:10.080 --> 13:10.919
Don't worry about it.

312
13:11.080 --> 13:12.320
From now on, I'll do whatever you say.

313
13:12.320 --> 13:13.159
Wherever you point, that's where I'll go.

314
13:14.519 --> 13:15.440
I'm heading to Qingzhou now.

315
13:15.559 --> 13:16.360
Then I'll come with you.

316
13:16.799 --> 13:17.279
No need.

317
13:18.039 --> 13:18.519
Alright.

318
13:18.879 --> 13:19.919
Just stay safe.

319
13:20.240 --> 13:21.159
If I can't reach you for two hours,

320
13:21.159 --> 13:21.840
I'm calling the cops.

321
13:21.919 --> 13:22.639
Dramatic.

322
13:23.440 --> 13:24.039
We'll talk when I'm back.

323
13:47.519 --> 13:48.320
Anyone home?

324
13:51.480 --> 13:52.480
Who are you looking for?

325
13:55.440 --> 13:56.679
I was just about to head out,

326
13:57.000 --> 13:57.799
and here you are.

327
13:57.879 --> 13:58.720
Come on in.

328
13:58.879 --> 14:00.960
My grandson Xuelin,

329
14:01.519 --> 14:03.279
is really something, you know?

330
14:04.039 --> 14:06.879
Even got a reporter here to interview him.

331
14:08.000 --> 14:09.080
Come on, sit right here.

332
14:09.240 --> 14:09.639
Have a seat.

333
14:10.399 --> 14:11.279
Make yourself at home.

334
14:11.879 --> 14:13.440
Let me get you some water.

335
14:13.639 --> 14:14.879
On such a freezing day,

336
14:14.879 --> 14:16.080
coming all this way.

337
14:16.360 --> 14:17.200
Thank you.

338
14:17.440 --> 14:17.879
Sit here.

339
14:18.360 --> 14:19.159
Go ahead, sit, sit.

340
14:19.159 --> 14:19.720
All right, take a seat.

341
14:29.879 --> 14:30.759
Here, have some water.

342
14:31.519 --> 14:31.840
Here you go.

343
14:33.200 --> 14:33.919
Thank you.

344
14:34.799 --> 14:35.720
Looking at photos?

345
14:37.440 --> 14:38.399
There are more here.

346
14:40.000 --> 14:40.759
Lots of them.

347
14:40.759 --> 14:42.120
They're all family photos of his.

348
14:42.120 --> 14:43.200
They turned out great.

349
14:43.879 --> 14:44.399
Take a look.

350
14:48.120 --> 14:49.279
Look how cute he was as a kid.

351
14:53.840 --> 14:56.000
The boy's had a rough life, really.

352
14:57.200 --> 14:57.639
You know...

353
14:58.039 --> 14:59.679
His dad was busy all day,

354
14:59.759 --> 15:00.879
rushing off his feet.

355
15:00.879 --> 15:02.120
Nobody looked after the boy.

356
15:02.360 --> 15:03.039
So just like that,

357
15:03.200 --> 15:05.159
he was sent over to stay with me.

358
15:05.480 --> 15:07.519
I didn't have fancy food either.

359
15:08.080 --> 15:09.519
I just made corn grits porridge.

360
15:10.080 --> 15:12.600
Eating that corn grits porridge, he said,

361
15:12.960 --> 15:14.000
"This stuff of yours,

362
15:14.000 --> 15:15.200
it scratches my throat.

363
15:15.679 --> 15:17.279
I can't swallow it," you know?

364
15:20.919 --> 15:23.440
It really cracked me up!

365
15:23.879 --> 15:25.679
He ate so slowly.

366
15:25.799 --> 15:27.200
When I nagged him a bit,

367
15:27.759 --> 15:28.519
oh boy,

368
15:28.879 --> 15:29.720
he started crying.

369
15:30.679 --> 15:32.360
He was very proud.

370
15:32.360 --> 15:33.720
Couldn't take any criticism.

371
15:37.120 --> 15:38.039
Grandma, here.

372
15:38.279 --> 15:38.919
Sit here.

373
15:38.919 --> 15:39.240
Please, have a seat.

374
15:39.240 --> 15:40.159
I'm interviewing you, look at me...

375
15:40.200 --> 15:40.720
Please sit down.

376
15:40.720 --> 15:41.600
You're interviewing me?

377
15:41.600 --> 15:41.960
Yes.

378
15:42.240 --> 15:42.600
Alright.

379
15:42.639 --> 15:43.120
Please sit, take a seat.

380
15:43.120 --> 15:44.200
Let's have a nice chat.

381
15:44.600 --> 15:44.919
Come on.

382
15:46.639 --> 15:47.840
Mrs. Gao, I'll take some notes, okay?

383
15:48.080 --> 15:48.360
Sure.

384
15:51.840 --> 15:53.759
What was Gao Xuelin's personality like?

385
15:54.120 --> 15:55.279
He didn't talk much.

386
15:55.480 --> 15:56.799
Even though he stayed quiet

387
15:56.799 --> 15:57.840
and kept to himself,

388
15:57.840 --> 15:59.320
he had quite a mind of his own.

389
16:00.080 --> 16:02.080
Did he go to school locally?

390
16:02.559 --> 16:04.320
He went to college right here.

391
16:04.720 --> 16:05.720
Didn't go elsewhere.

392
16:06.159 --> 16:08.399
Has he been to Lacheng, then?

393
16:08.840 --> 16:09.480
Him?

394
16:09.799 --> 16:11.480
He went to Lacheng all the time!

395
16:11.480 --> 16:12.480
Good grief,

396
16:12.480 --> 16:13.600
non-stop!

397
16:13.600 --> 16:14.600
You wouldn't believe it.

398
16:14.600 --> 16:15.679
What did he go there for?

399
16:16.000 --> 16:16.679
For what?

400
16:16.679 --> 16:17.679
He wouldn't let anyone ask!

401
16:18.559 --> 16:19.399
If you asked,

402
16:19.399 --> 16:20.559
he'd get upset.

403
16:20.840 --> 16:21.840
He always told me,

404
16:22.559 --> 16:24.360
"Don't bother worrying about it."

405
16:26.080 --> 16:26.960
That's what he'd say.

406
16:29.320 --> 16:30.480
It's only because you're here...

407
16:31.879 --> 16:32.399
Mrs. Gao,

408
16:33.639 --> 16:35.080
I was looking at the photos earlier.

409
16:36.159 --> 16:36.799
Um...

410
16:37.080 --> 16:38.639
Gao Xuelin's mother,

411
16:38.679 --> 16:39.480
which

412
16:39.639 --> 16:40.399
one was she?

413
16:40.759 --> 16:41.399
I'll find it for you.

414
16:41.639 --> 16:42.200
Here it is.

415
16:44.519 --> 16:45.000
This one.

416
16:45.799 --> 16:46.360
Take a look.

417
16:47.120 --> 16:49.360
She was such a gorgeous woman.

418
16:50.759 --> 16:52.120
And such a good person too.

419
16:52.360 --> 16:54.000
Giving birth to him, though,

420
16:55.200 --> 16:56.279
she suffered massive bleeding.

421
16:56.960 --> 16:58.159
Just like that, she was gone.

422
16:58.600 --> 17:00.480
It broke my heart so much.

423
17:06.920 --> 17:07.720
And...

424
17:07.960 --> 17:09.839
what about Gao Xuelin's father?

425
17:13.759 --> 17:17.119
His father was a taxi driver.

426
17:17.720 --> 17:19.279
Got into a car crash that year,

427
17:19.519 --> 17:20.400
and passed away too.

428
17:27.720 --> 17:28.319
Child,

429
17:29.559 --> 17:30.720
remember this:

430
17:30.960 --> 17:33.519
never drink and drive.

431
17:33.519 --> 17:34.920
It's devastating!

432
17:37.200 --> 17:37.640
Right.

433
17:47.759 --> 17:49.359
Since you're here today,

434
17:49.599 --> 17:50.720
I won't stand on ceremony.

435
17:51.480 --> 17:52.720
I'd like to ask you a favor.

436
17:54.319 --> 17:55.000
Go ahead.

437
17:55.319 --> 17:57.920
You see that big smokestack on the east end?

438
17:58.519 --> 17:59.880
The factory's gone,

439
17:59.880 --> 18:00.640
all shut down,

440
18:00.640 --> 18:02.680
yet that smokestack is still standing.

441
18:02.920 --> 18:03.519
You...

442
18:03.839 --> 18:07.079
You meet a lot of big shots,

443
18:07.319 --> 18:09.039
and you can talk to them.

444
18:09.680 --> 18:11.079
Tell those officials

445
18:11.519 --> 18:12.880
to tear down that smokestack.

446
18:13.599 --> 18:14.200
Could you?

447
18:14.720 --> 18:15.119
Grandma...

448
18:15.119 --> 18:15.440
Can you?

449
18:15.440 --> 18:18.480
You want me to report on that smokestack?

450
18:18.480 --> 18:19.279
No.

451
18:20.599 --> 18:23.920
Don't you deal with big shots all the time?

452
18:24.599 --> 18:26.400
Where else am I supposed to find them?

453
18:28.240 --> 18:29.359
Tearing down a smokestack,

454
18:29.359 --> 18:31.240
how hard could that be for them?

455
18:31.559 --> 18:35.440
You... you even wrote an article on Xuelin.

456
18:39.839 --> 18:40.400
Mrs. Gao,

457
18:41.920 --> 18:43.400
where does Xuelin stay?

458
18:43.680 --> 18:45.079
Can I take a look inside his room?

459
18:45.519 --> 18:46.480
It's right in that room.

460
18:46.480 --> 18:47.839
Come on, I'll show you.

461
18:55.400 --> 18:55.880
Take a look.

462
18:55.880 --> 18:57.039
This is his room.

463
19:02.319 --> 19:03.720
You rest here, okay?

464
19:03.759 --> 19:05.519
I'll make you pickled cabbage dumplings,

465
19:05.559 --> 19:06.079
how about that?

466
19:06.359 --> 19:07.440
Don't trouble yourself.

467
19:08.039 --> 19:08.440
Don't worry about it.

468
19:08.640 --> 19:09.559
Come on, have a seat.

469
21:29.440 --> 21:31.720
Dad, I got you!

470
21:36.519 --> 21:37.759
Dad, I won!

471
21:45.839 --> 21:46.720
Good job.

472
21:49.599 --> 21:51.279
Dad, aren't you eating?

473
21:51.359 --> 21:53.519
Daddy's got a big job to run today.

474
21:53.559 --> 21:54.480
To make some good money.

475
21:54.759 --> 21:56.880
I'll buy you a big toy gun when I'm back.

476
21:56.880 --> 21:58.480
Yay!

477
21:59.359 --> 22:00.480
Will you be back tonight?

478
22:00.759 --> 22:01.519
You bet.

479
22:01.960 --> 22:03.200
We've gotta spend New Year's together.

480
22:03.720 --> 22:04.279
Okay!

481
22:04.279 --> 22:04.799
Go on inside.

482
22:04.880 --> 22:05.920
Eat with Grandma, okay?

483
22:06.720 --> 22:07.880
Come back soon!

484
22:08.079 --> 22:08.599
Will do.

485
22:15.359 --> 22:16.200
Dad!

486
22:17.240 --> 22:19.759
Grandma told me to give you a meat bun.

487
22:35.559 --> 22:36.480
Did you find his place?

488
22:38.799 --> 22:40.279
Was the tip I gave you useful?

489
22:40.680 --> 22:41.599
Find anything new?

490
22:48.079 --> 22:50.839
December 31, 1999.

491
22:51.160 --> 22:54.559
Beer taster Liu Xuemei froze to death after drinking.

492
22:55.240 --> 22:58.200
December 31, 1999.

493
22:58.720 --> 23:00.799
Taxi driver Gao so-and-so

494
23:00.920 --> 23:02.279
died in a drunk driving crash. Hello?

495
23:02.640 --> 23:03.200
Hello?

496
23:04.279 --> 23:05.200
Are you listening?

497
23:05.200 --> 23:08.200
They actually died on the very same day.

498
23:09.880 --> 23:10.440
Hello?

499
23:14.839 --> 23:16.160
Could that really be a coincidence?

500
23:16.799 --> 23:17.839
What did you find?

501
23:17.839 --> 23:18.640
I'll tell you when I get back.

502
23:20.480 --> 23:21.559
Liu Xuemei...

503
23:22.680 --> 23:24.440
What really happened that day?

504
23:32.680 --> 23:34.839
Xuemei! Xuemei!

505
23:36.000 --> 23:36.599
Leshui.

506
23:36.720 --> 23:37.519
Xuemei!

507
23:37.759 --> 23:38.640
You made it.

508
23:40.319 --> 23:41.720
I took a cab from Qingzhou.

509
23:42.160 --> 23:42.839
That's great.

510
23:43.200 --> 23:44.480
Hurry and go inside, Xuemei.

511
23:44.559 --> 23:45.480
I'll wait for your good news.

512
23:49.079 --> 23:50.039
Good luck, Xuemei!

513
24:06.920 --> 24:07.319
Shen!

514
24:09.440 --> 24:10.119
Let me take that.

515
24:10.119 --> 24:10.559
I've got it.

516
24:11.240 --> 24:12.319
Why take a train at this hour?

517
24:12.319 --> 24:12.799
I was in a rush.

518
24:12.960 --> 24:13.880
Caught the earliest one.

519
24:13.920 --> 24:14.799
What's the big rush?

520
24:14.920 --> 24:15.480
Let's talk in the car.

521
24:16.119 --> 24:16.599
Right here.

522
24:17.039 --> 24:17.640
Get in.

523
24:23.880 --> 24:24.799
I was wrong before.

524
24:25.559 --> 24:26.559
He's investigating this

525
24:27.200 --> 24:29.119
because he suspects Gao Wusong's death

526
24:29.279 --> 24:30.519
was tied to Liu Xuemei.

527
24:31.079 --> 24:32.000
His real target

528
24:32.279 --> 24:33.759
were the tapes I shot back then.

529
24:34.079 --> 24:35.400
He definitely stole those videotapes.

530
24:36.640 --> 24:38.160
Now I know why he stole them too.

531
24:38.400 --> 24:39.440
He suspects Liu Xuemei

532
24:39.440 --> 24:40.519
was riding in his dad's car.

533
24:45.039 --> 24:46.400
I found this at his place.

534
24:47.240 --> 24:48.200
I checked with the auction house.

535
24:48.680 --> 24:50.680
They said in '99, to mark the millennium,

536
24:50.880 --> 24:52.119
they made custom bidding paddles.

537
24:52.640 --> 24:53.880
On December 31st,

538
24:53.880 --> 24:55.119
Gao Wusong went to Lacheng.

539
24:55.519 --> 24:57.680
Lacheng only had one auction that day.

540
24:59.359 --> 25:00.200
So he suspects

541
25:00.200 --> 25:02.160
his dad drove Liu Xuemei that day.

542
25:02.160 --> 25:02.640
Right.

543
25:03.640 --> 25:04.440
At least,

544
25:04.599 --> 25:05.920
that's what Gao Xuelin thinks.

545
25:06.039 --> 25:06.839
He even tracked down

546
25:06.839 --> 25:08.599
a matching paddle from that auction.

547
25:09.400 --> 25:10.839
It's probably not Liu Xuemei's paddle,

548
25:11.079 --> 25:12.160
but it clearly shows

549
25:12.160 --> 25:13.480
Gao Xuelin's line of investigation.

550
25:15.640 --> 25:17.119
Is Liu Xuemei's death

551
25:17.200 --> 25:19.000
tied to Gao Wusong?

552
25:19.680 --> 25:20.720
Or

553
25:21.599 --> 25:23.400
were they murdered together?

554
25:24.400 --> 25:27.839
Liu Xuemei's death is tied to a cop's dad.

555
25:28.319 --> 25:28.920
Shen,

556
25:29.279 --> 25:30.720
this is huge news.

557
25:31.119 --> 25:32.119
It could easily make front page.

558
25:35.039 --> 25:35.480
Let's go.

559
25:38.079 --> 25:39.319
A serial murder case...

560
25:40.599 --> 25:42.319
Could it be linked to the past?

561
25:44.400 --> 25:45.240
How did they die?

562
25:46.000 --> 25:48.480
They're all the old-timers from back then.

563
25:49.240 --> 25:50.599
They moved out later on.

564
25:50.599 --> 25:51.200
Officer Gao.

565
25:51.480 --> 25:52.440
Got a minute to talk?

566
25:53.359 --> 25:55.759
Anything else you saw or noticed,

567
25:55.759 --> 25:56.440
feel free to tell us.

568
25:58.319 --> 25:59.160
Think carefully about it.

569
25:59.160 --> 25:59.960
I thought about it, but didn't notice anything.

570
25:59.960 --> 26:00.559
Right?

571
26:01.559 --> 26:02.240
Well,

572
26:02.759 --> 26:03.519
if you happen to recall

573
26:03.519 --> 26:05.759
any details later on,

574
26:05.759 --> 26:06.240
or anything at all,

575
26:06.519 --> 26:07.720
just get in touch with us.

576
26:08.400 --> 26:09.799
Did you spot any suspicious people?

577
26:09.799 --> 26:10.759
No, not at all.

578
26:11.519 --> 26:12.240
I moved out long ago.

579
26:12.559 --> 26:13.559
Haven't lived here in ages.

580
26:16.079 --> 26:16.920
I don't know the details.

581
26:16.920 --> 26:18.279
Please give it some more thought.

582
26:55.480 --> 26:56.240
Reporter Shen.

583
26:56.519 --> 26:57.880
Qingzhou is colder than Lacheng, right?

584
26:59.559 --> 27:00.079
It's all right.

585
27:00.720 --> 27:01.720
Your grandma was very welcoming.

586
27:04.559 --> 27:05.759
Investigating at my place,

587
27:06.160 --> 27:07.200
did you find anything new?

588
27:09.200 --> 27:11.000
Any progress on the break-in at my place?

589
27:11.359 --> 27:11.920
We're still looking into it.

590
27:13.519 --> 27:14.079
Real efficient.

591
27:15.519 --> 27:16.039
Tell you what.

592
27:16.960 --> 27:18.640
Let me first share some of

593
27:19.319 --> 27:20.519
the things I uncovered.

594
27:24.759 --> 27:26.279
Your father was Gao Wusong.

595
27:26.839 --> 27:27.920
A taxi driver.

596
27:28.359 --> 27:29.799
Born in 1964.

597
27:30.359 --> 27:32.400
On December 31, 1999,

598
27:32.599 --> 27:34.119
he died in a traffic accident.

599
27:35.000 --> 27:36.119
He was only 36.

600
27:36.440 --> 27:38.920
The crash happened on Ring Road in Lacheng.

601
27:39.799 --> 27:41.960
That day, he took a long-distance fare.

602
27:42.400 --> 27:45.079
A woman rushed from Qingzhou to Lacheng

603
27:45.079 --> 27:46.519
to attend an auction.

604
27:47.160 --> 27:49.720
The passenger's name was Liu Xuemei.

605
27:51.319 --> 27:52.279
I checked the gas stations

606
27:52.279 --> 27:53.880
along the route from Qingzhou to Lacheng.

607
27:54.519 --> 27:57.079
An old employee recognized your father.

608
27:58.039 --> 27:59.079
That day, he saw

609
27:59.079 --> 28:01.119
a pretty female passenger sitting in the car.

610
28:02.599 --> 28:03.599
Have something hot to eat.

611
28:04.799 --> 28:05.440
Thank you.

612
28:06.119 --> 28:07.400
We've still got a long way to go.

613
28:22.640 --> 28:23.519
That night, Liu Xuemei

614
28:23.519 --> 28:25.400
was at a phone booth on Xingfu Road

615
28:25.920 --> 28:27.720
and died of hypothermia after drinking.

616
28:28.559 --> 28:30.079
Your father, on Huandao Road,

617
28:30.079 --> 28:31.920
died from drunk driving.

618
28:32.480 --> 28:34.079
They died on the very same day,

619
28:34.400 --> 28:35.519
both drunk.

620
28:40.000 --> 28:40.640
What else?

621
28:44.359 --> 28:46.599
There are two reasons you care about Liu Xuemei's death.

622
28:47.200 --> 28:47.839
First,

623
28:48.279 --> 28:50.759
your dad and Liu Xuemei argued in the car,

624
28:51.480 --> 28:53.599
which ended up causing her death,

625
28:54.000 --> 28:55.799
and then your father got into a car crash.

626
28:56.640 --> 28:57.920
Maybe someone at the brewery

627
28:57.920 --> 28:59.319
found out about what happened,

628
29:00.079 --> 29:00.799
so

629
29:01.319 --> 29:03.799
you're covering up the truth for your father.

630
29:05.039 --> 29:05.720
Second,

631
29:06.480 --> 29:07.759
Liu Xuemei did something

632
29:08.319 --> 29:10.000
that caused your father's car crash,

633
29:10.079 --> 29:11.119
and this whole thing

634
29:11.319 --> 29:12.799
was tied to the brewery buyout.

635
29:13.200 --> 29:15.279
So you're tracking down everyone involved.

636
29:15.519 --> 29:17.559
Then I suddenly dug into this case,

637
29:17.799 --> 29:19.559
and you thought my discarded footage

638
29:19.559 --> 29:21.039
held secrets from back then.

639
29:21.559 --> 29:22.279
That's why

640
29:23.200 --> 29:25.039
you stole my tapes.

641
29:38.000 --> 29:39.680
Spoken like a true award-winning reporter.

642
29:40.839 --> 29:41.680
Nice story you spun.

643
29:42.160 --> 29:43.119
Trying to bait me, huh?

644
29:44.400 --> 29:45.039
You

645
29:45.039 --> 29:46.480
didn't even give me a heads-up

646
29:46.880 --> 29:48.039
before showing up at my place

647
29:48.519 --> 29:49.519
and bothering my grandma.

648
29:50.039 --> 29:50.799
A bit out of line, isn't it?

649
29:52.440 --> 29:53.200
In here,

650
29:53.200 --> 29:55.400
there might be leads on the burglary at your place.

651
29:56.319 --> 29:57.240
I'll take it back to look into it.

652
29:57.359 --> 29:58.000
I'll return it when I'm done.

653
29:59.079 --> 30:00.480
Didn't you see it last time?

654
30:01.079 --> 30:02.480
Why didn't you report it to your bosses?

655
30:03.359 --> 30:04.319
Got a guilty conscience?

656
30:04.640 --> 30:06.160
I have no idea what you're talking about.

657
30:08.519 --> 30:09.480
Give me back the tape.

658
30:09.960 --> 30:12.039
Just because I wanted to see your tape,

659
30:12.160 --> 30:13.279
you can't say I stole it.

660
30:13.799 --> 30:14.880
Isn't that just framing me?

661
30:23.799 --> 30:24.799
Here's my phone number.

662
30:25.400 --> 30:26.920
It's on 24/7.

663
30:27.279 --> 30:29.039
So if you have questions, just ask me directly.

664
30:37.440 --> 30:38.759
They're almost done questioning downstairs.

665
31:03.359 --> 31:04.160
Eat, eat, eat.

666
31:05.640 --> 31:06.440
You're back?

667
31:07.599 --> 31:09.119
Isn't she the one who filmed us?

668
31:09.119 --> 31:09.960
Reporter Shen?

669
31:09.960 --> 31:10.880
It really is her.

670
31:11.680 --> 31:12.400
Mr. Sun.

671
31:13.039 --> 31:13.680
Mr. Li.

672
31:14.759 --> 31:15.359
Mr. Ge.

673
31:16.920 --> 31:17.640
Reporter Shen!

674
31:17.640 --> 31:18.359
After all these years,

675
31:18.359 --> 31:20.000
you still remember us old guys?

676
31:20.079 --> 31:20.960
How could I forget?

677
31:20.960 --> 31:21.839
Of course I remember you.

678
31:21.839 --> 31:22.920
Look, you've lost your teeth.

679
31:22.920 --> 31:23.759
What's become of you?

680
31:23.759 --> 31:24.480
I remember you, too.

681
31:24.480 --> 31:25.200
Stop ragging on me.

682
31:25.200 --> 31:25.920
Look at you.

683
31:26.160 --> 31:26.839
What happened to you?

684
31:27.079 --> 31:27.759
You're totally bald!

685
31:28.039 --> 31:29.000
Bald as can be.

686
31:30.119 --> 31:31.200
Don't pick on Old Ge.

687
31:31.480 --> 31:31.759
Look at you,

688
31:31.759 --> 31:34.200
your hair's too thin to even mention.

689
31:34.920 --> 31:35.559
What are you doing?

690
31:35.599 --> 31:37.000
A pretty reporter is right here.

691
31:37.000 --> 31:37.839
Mind your manners!

692
31:38.480 --> 31:39.119
I forgot for a second.

693
31:39.119 --> 31:39.759
Let me fix it.

694
31:42.200 --> 31:43.279
Reporter Shen.

695
31:44.359 --> 31:45.200
Director Cheng.

696
31:45.599 --> 31:46.480
Long time no see.

697
31:47.279 --> 31:48.480
I haven't been director for years.

698
31:48.759 --> 31:49.759
How's your health?

699
31:50.160 --> 31:51.079
Good, very good.

700
31:52.119 --> 31:53.079
When did you get back?

701
31:53.359 --> 31:54.200
Just a couple of days ago.

702
31:57.920 --> 31:59.279
You say the days are long,

703
31:59.279 --> 32:00.480
so I pass the liquor along.

704
32:01.200 --> 32:01.640
How's that?

705
32:02.720 --> 32:04.000
Great, damn great!

706
32:04.319 --> 32:05.200
I made that up myself.

707
32:07.200 --> 32:07.880
Well, you see,

708
32:08.039 --> 32:08.920
after we got laid off,

709
32:09.279 --> 32:10.359
us old guys

710
32:10.400 --> 32:12.039
had nowhere to drink and chat.

711
32:13.240 --> 32:13.799
So we

712
32:13.799 --> 32:14.920
took this rundown place,

713
32:14.920 --> 32:15.920
cleaned it all up,

714
32:16.680 --> 32:18.039
and gave these drunks a place to hang out.

715
32:19.079 --> 32:21.880
Outsiders call it Old Drunkards' Paradise,

716
32:22.880 --> 32:24.920
but we call it Old Workmates' Paradise.

717
32:26.640 --> 32:26.920
Come on.

718
32:27.119 --> 32:28.039
Come on inside, please.

719
32:28.119 --> 32:28.839
Right this way.

720
32:29.079 --> 32:29.759
There's a seat here!

721
32:29.759 --> 32:30.559
Sit here and drink with us!

722
32:30.759 --> 32:31.240
Reporter Shen,

723
32:32.359 --> 32:32.960
have a drink, have some!

724
32:32.960 --> 32:33.960
Can't you shut your trap?

725
32:34.119 --> 32:34.759
Go easy on the booze.

726
32:34.839 --> 32:35.319
Jianguo!

727
32:36.400 --> 32:37.319
The stove is still burning.

728
32:37.400 --> 32:37.960
Keep an eye on it for me.

729
32:38.319 --> 32:38.799
You got it!

730
32:39.519 --> 32:39.960
Have a seat over here.

731
32:41.000 --> 32:42.119
It's a bit quieter in this room.

732
32:43.599 --> 32:44.279
What would you like to eat?

733
32:44.440 --> 32:45.039
I'll whip something up for you.

734
32:45.359 --> 32:46.240
I've already eaten.

735
32:46.880 --> 32:48.119
I just wanted to visit you

736
32:48.720 --> 32:49.759
and catch up a bit.

737
32:50.920 --> 32:51.400
All right, then.

738
32:52.359 --> 32:53.039
I'll brew a pot of tea.

739
32:53.920 --> 32:54.359
Have a seat.

740
32:54.440 --> 32:55.039
Thank you.

741
32:55.359 --> 32:55.799
Sit down.

742
33:14.880 --> 33:15.480
Come on in.

743
33:19.400 --> 33:20.359
Have a seat, sit down.

744
33:22.039 --> 33:22.680
Well, uh...

745
33:22.799 --> 33:23.599
Thank you, thank you.

746
33:23.599 --> 33:24.839
Please, don't trouble yourself.

747
33:25.279 --> 33:26.119
The tea isn't anything special.

748
33:26.279 --> 33:27.400
Just make do with it.

749
33:30.599 --> 33:31.359
Please sit, please.

750
33:38.039 --> 33:38.759
So...

751
33:40.200 --> 33:41.079
you coming to see me,

752
33:42.480 --> 33:43.240
you must have a reason.

753
33:45.319 --> 33:46.759
Then I'll just cut to the chase.

754
33:49.400 --> 33:50.640
The recent murders...

755
33:51.359 --> 33:52.640
you've heard about them?

756
33:54.720 --> 33:55.480
I have.

757
33:57.160 --> 33:58.160
Do you think

758
33:59.000 --> 34:01.119
they have to do with

759
34:01.240 --> 34:02.240
selling the factory back then?

760
34:08.360 --> 34:09.639
If I said they didn't,

761
34:10.400 --> 34:11.199
would you believe me?

762
34:14.000 --> 34:15.039
Don't know who it is,

763
34:15.599 --> 34:16.440
or what's gotten into them,

764
34:17.159 --> 34:18.239
after all these years,

765
34:18.400 --> 34:20.000
losing their minds doing this.

766
34:21.840 --> 34:22.679
Let me tell you,

767
34:23.159 --> 34:24.559
us old-timers,

768
34:25.400 --> 34:26.079
our consciences are clear.

769
34:29.039 --> 34:30.159
Do the other old workers

770
34:30.519 --> 34:31.559
come around here often too?

771
34:33.559 --> 34:34.679
Haipeng and his crowd do.

772
34:35.360 --> 34:37.360
Those old bastards are here every day.

773
34:40.039 --> 34:40.719
Well,

774
34:41.039 --> 34:44.440
has anyone else asked about back then?

775
34:45.760 --> 34:46.360
Actually, yes.

776
34:46.920 --> 34:47.639
Who?

777
34:48.159 --> 34:48.800
A cop.

778
34:49.840 --> 34:51.039
The police came by.

779
34:52.320 --> 34:53.360
Older or young?

780
34:54.639 --> 34:55.480
A young kid.

781
34:56.719 --> 34:57.440
Said his name

782
34:58.199 --> 34:58.800
was Gao.

783
34:59.800 --> 35:00.320
You know him?

784
35:01.360 --> 35:03.039
Did he ask about Liu Xuemei?

785
35:03.519 --> 35:04.719
And what happened the day she died?

786
35:05.159 --> 35:06.400
That's exactly what he asked.

787
35:11.400 --> 35:12.800
That's all ancient history.

788
35:13.800 --> 35:14.559
In a flash,

789
35:15.440 --> 35:17.000
over ten years have gone by.

790
35:22.840 --> 35:23.280
Whose turn?

791
35:23.960 --> 35:24.920
You play. Go on, play.

792
35:25.400 --> 35:25.679
Me?

793
35:25.679 --> 35:26.280
Hold on, don't rush.

794
35:26.280 --> 35:27.079
All right, look at this!

795
35:27.679 --> 35:28.119
How about that?

796
35:28.599 --> 35:29.320
Damn good!

797
35:29.480 --> 35:30.079
Three 2s.

798
35:30.880 --> 35:31.320
Hey, hey, you...

799
35:31.320 --> 35:31.760
Pass, pass, pass.

800
35:31.760 --> 35:32.880
Can't beat it, pass!

801
35:32.960 --> 35:33.320
Pass.

802
35:33.639 --> 35:34.119
Come on...

803
35:34.159 --> 35:34.679
Can't beat that.

804
35:34.840 --> 35:35.800
Pass.

805
35:36.760 --> 35:37.480
Three 2s!

806
35:37.519 --> 35:38.360
I win!

807
35:38.719 --> 35:39.639
You guys...

808
35:41.159 --> 35:41.559
What in the world...

809
35:41.559 --> 35:42.159
How could you play like that?

810
35:42.639 --> 35:43.599
In the first three quarters,

811
35:43.719 --> 35:44.639
our bottling workshop

812
35:44.840 --> 35:45.800
came in first again!

813
35:46.400 --> 35:47.679
Great!

814
35:47.840 --> 35:48.360
Old Cheng,

815
35:48.400 --> 35:50.199
you led the way wonderfully!

816
35:50.199 --> 35:50.760
Didn't he?

817
35:51.320 --> 35:52.440
Absolutely!

818
35:53.039 --> 35:54.119
Director Tian from the Women's Federation

819
35:54.239 --> 35:55.440
has taken great care of us.

820
35:55.480 --> 35:56.079
Right?

821
35:56.360 --> 35:57.320
Just doing my job. Come on,

822
35:57.960 --> 36:00.320
let's toast Director Tian!

823
36:00.920 --> 36:01.400
Cheers!

824
36:01.719 --> 36:03.000
Director Tian, thank you so much!

825
36:03.719 --> 36:04.400
As for labor protection gear,

826
36:04.400 --> 36:05.199
hand out extra to everyone!

827
36:05.320 --> 36:06.320
Count on it.

828
36:06.320 --> 36:06.559
Cheers!

829
36:06.599 --> 36:07.679
Thank you, everyone! Thank you!

830
36:09.119 --> 36:10.119
Bottoms up! Bottoms up!

831
36:57.519 --> 36:58.480
Alright, everyone,

832
36:59.199 --> 37:00.239
let me introduce someone to you.

833
37:00.920 --> 37:02.599
Our factory's new beer taster,

834
37:03.280 --> 37:04.199
Comrade Liu Xuemei.

835
37:05.159 --> 37:05.719
Give her a hand!

836
37:06.679 --> 37:07.519
Welcome, Xuemei!

837
37:08.760 --> 37:11.119
Welcome! Welcome, welcome!

838
37:11.239 --> 37:12.039
Now, Xuemei,

839
37:13.039 --> 37:13.639
it's your first day here.

840
37:14.360 --> 37:15.320
Well,

841
37:15.880 --> 37:16.480
now that you're in the workshop,

842
37:17.239 --> 37:18.079
we're all family.

843
37:18.440 --> 37:19.519
If you run into any trouble, just speak up.

844
37:19.880 --> 37:22.079
We older folks will take care of you.

845
37:22.199 --> 37:22.960
Don't you worry.

846
37:24.280 --> 37:25.599
And, uh...

847
37:26.000 --> 37:26.679
there's one more thing.

848
37:27.280 --> 37:27.719
What is it?

849
37:28.880 --> 37:29.679
How should I put it?

850
37:30.000 --> 37:30.599
What's the matter?

851
37:33.599 --> 37:35.159
Lao Cheng, you're utterly hopeless.

852
37:35.639 --> 37:36.199
I'll say it for you.

853
37:40.119 --> 37:40.760
Xuemei,

854
37:42.239 --> 37:44.039
that little skirt looks gorgeous on you.

855
37:44.639 --> 37:45.920
If I had your figure,

856
37:46.440 --> 37:47.400
I'd wear one every day too.

857
37:47.480 --> 37:48.800
Too bad you don't!

858
37:49.280 --> 37:49.960
What did you say?

859
37:49.960 --> 37:50.840
Get out of here!

860
37:52.599 --> 37:53.159
Xuemei,

861
37:53.679 --> 37:54.679
the thing is,

862
37:54.760 --> 37:55.880
our workshop has rules.

863
37:56.079 --> 37:57.360
Once you're in the workshop,

864
37:57.519 --> 37:58.639
you have to wear the uniform.

865
37:59.239 --> 37:59.679
Look,

866
37:59.880 --> 38:01.400
don't our work clothes look sharp?

867
38:01.400 --> 38:01.880
Right?

868
38:03.039 --> 38:04.760
I just thought, since it's my first day...

869
38:06.000 --> 38:06.840
It's my fault.

870
38:07.320 --> 38:08.599
I didn't check beforehand.

871
38:09.480 --> 38:10.599
I'm so sorry, everyone.

872
38:22.840 --> 38:23.320
Nice!

873
38:23.719 --> 38:24.280
Great!

874
38:26.000 --> 38:26.760
What are you doing?

875
38:27.280 --> 38:28.360
You're not a beer taster.

876
38:29.400 --> 38:29.840
Come on, come on.

877
38:29.840 --> 38:30.559
Raise your glasses, pick 'em up!

878
38:30.679 --> 38:31.519
Come on, Xuemei.

879
38:31.639 --> 38:32.360
Come on, everyone.

880
38:32.719 --> 38:33.440
Come on.

881
38:34.960 --> 38:36.119
We're all family here.

882
38:36.400 --> 38:38.320
Let's welcome Liu Xuemei!

883
38:38.639 --> 38:40.400
Welcome, Liu Xuemei!

884
38:40.400 --> 38:42.079
Welcome, Liu Xuemei!

885
38:42.360 --> 38:43.519
Cheers!

886
38:53.559 --> 38:54.840
Just because a woman came by,

887
38:55.039 --> 38:55.840
you're getting restless already?

888
38:55.960 --> 38:57.760
We're just worried you can't sit still.

889
38:58.000 --> 38:58.760
Why would I be restless?

890
39:00.840 --> 39:02.880
Your wife left with the kid two years ago,

891
39:03.199 --> 39:05.239
and she hasn't come back since.

892
39:06.079 --> 39:07.159
You just have to run your mouth, huh?

893
39:08.199 --> 39:09.559
I've only got myself to feed.

894
39:09.920 --> 39:10.760
Who gives a damn anyway?

895
39:11.880 --> 39:12.400
Director,

896
39:12.639 --> 39:13.719
cut the act.

897
39:13.960 --> 39:16.320
We all know Liu Xuemei is divorced too.

898
39:16.599 --> 39:17.880
Quit playing coy.

899
39:17.880 --> 39:19.400
You two should just get together.

900
39:19.760 --> 39:20.639
You'd get a ready-made son,

901
39:20.800 --> 39:21.679
how great is that?

902
39:22.119 --> 39:22.719
Yeah, yeah, right.

903
39:23.559 --> 39:24.039
Laughing?

904
39:24.320 --> 39:25.039
What are you laughing at?

905
39:25.559 --> 39:26.360
What's so funny?

906
39:27.480 --> 39:27.880
Get back to work.

907
39:27.880 --> 39:28.239
What's wrong?

908
39:28.559 --> 39:29.360
I'm going.

909
39:29.360 --> 39:29.960
Go on, get to work.

910
39:29.960 --> 39:30.360
I...

911
39:31.320 --> 39:32.440
Wait, wait, we'll wait for you!

912
39:33.239 --> 39:33.920
Can't play cards without you!

913
39:33.920 --> 39:34.920
You guys have too much time on your hands.

914
39:43.400 --> 39:44.360
Xuemei, getting water?

915
39:44.360 --> 39:44.920
Xuemei.

916
39:45.800 --> 39:46.480
Have you eaten?

917
39:46.800 --> 39:47.360
I have.

918
39:48.199 --> 39:48.719
Xuemei.

919
39:49.119 --> 39:49.800
Mr. Cheng.

920
39:50.480 --> 39:51.159
Getting water?

921
39:52.159 --> 39:52.719
Xuemei.

922
40:15.199 --> 40:16.480
I forgot the tea leaves, Mr. Cheng.

923
40:16.679 --> 40:17.599
I'll go grab them from the workshop.

924
40:26.800 --> 40:27.920
It's not easy raising a kid on your own.

925
40:30.559 --> 40:31.000
It's fine.

926
40:31.280 --> 40:31.880
I'm used to it.

927
40:34.719 --> 40:35.360
Well...

928
40:35.639 --> 40:36.480
If you ever run into trouble,

929
40:37.159 --> 40:37.559
just say the word.

930
40:39.400 --> 40:40.400
Thanks, Mr. Cheng.

931
40:42.159 --> 40:43.079
The guys in the workshop,

932
40:43.800 --> 40:44.440
they're all pretty rough,

933
40:44.599 --> 40:45.519
but they've got good hearts.

934
40:46.440 --> 40:47.559
If there's any gossip going around,

935
40:48.199 --> 40:48.920
don't take it to heart.

936
40:50.039 --> 40:51.280
What gossip?

937
40:53.239 --> 40:53.679
Nothing?

938
40:55.960 --> 40:56.800
Well... all right then.

939
40:59.679 --> 41:00.960
It's just those punks,

940
41:02.639 --> 41:04.199
always teasing a bachelor like me.

941
41:05.079 --> 41:06.119
Whenever a woman comes around,

942
41:06.320 --> 41:07.239
they try to play matchmaker.

943
41:09.360 --> 41:10.440
Don't let it bother you.

944
41:11.679 --> 41:13.119
I wouldn't take it to heart.

945
41:13.559 --> 41:15.119
I can manage my own life.

946
41:15.719 --> 41:16.519
I don't have any intentions like that,

947
41:16.719 --> 41:17.440
so don't overthink it either.

948
41:17.960 --> 41:18.639
Didn't take it to heart, huh?

949
41:19.719 --> 41:20.039
Well,

950
41:20.239 --> 41:21.039
if you're not interested,

951
41:21.280 --> 41:21.960
that's a relief.

952
41:25.639 --> 41:26.199
Mr. Cheng,

953
41:26.639 --> 41:27.280
the water's overflowing.

954
41:34.039 --> 41:35.199
She's not interested,

955
41:39.280 --> 41:41.519
and now it feels off.

956
42:01.639 --> 42:02.159
What's wrong?

957
42:03.639 --> 42:04.199
No idea.

958
42:04.199 --> 42:04.800
Looks like he fell asleep.

959
42:34.679 --> 42:35.679
On the very same day,

960
42:36.519 --> 42:40.280
both died of alcohol poisoning.

961
42:40.519 --> 42:41.559
Don't you find that suspicious?

962
42:41.920 --> 42:43.400
Know what to say

963
42:44.000 --> 42:45.559
and what not to say.

964
42:46.480 --> 42:48.079
Whatever you do, don't slip up.

965
42:48.639 --> 42:50.519
This has nothing to do with my mentor.

966
42:50.760 --> 42:52.079
I apologize.

967
42:52.280 --> 42:53.679
I shouldn't have run my mouth.
